@startuml runtime_execution_control_store
title Durable Runtime Execution Control Store
' Java baseline: pi-mono-java 74f1b8314c9a5eb3d1659dfed2ab90b787dd647f
' CANCELED is implemented by the companion change, not present in the baseline.
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/RuntimeExecutionPersistenceService.java#appendEntry/appendEntryWithUsage/restoreCommittedTerminal
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/RuntimeExecutionPersistenceService.java
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/RuntimeExecutionControlRepository.java
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/MyBatisRuntimeExecutionControlRepository.java#markTerminal/cancelPendingDecisions
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/RuntimeSessionRepository.java
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/resources/mapper/session/RuntimeExecutionControlMapper.xml#cancelPendingConfirmations/cancelPendingPlanConfirmations/cancelPendingQuestionAnswers
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/resources/db/gaussdb/install/session_schema.sql
' Pi source baseline: pi 4af9d21d3b4d664e4a29fcabfec85171077248e3
' Pi source: packages/agent/src/agent-loop.ts#runAgentLoop and #prepareToolCall
' Observed behavior: claims check the exact execution and reject stopped executions.
' Design reason: one Spring transaction binds accepted events and terminal events to an exact execution segment.
' Design reason: terminal commit also cancels unclaimed decisions without deleting accepted user input.
' Java divergence: durable control and consumption cancellation are CampusClaw architecture changes.
class RuntimeExecutionPersistenceService {
  acceptMessage(...)
  acceptInterrupt(...)
  markToolConfirming(...)
  acceptToolConfirmation(...)
  acceptPlanConfirmation(...)
  acceptQuestionAnswer(...)
  commitTerminal(...)
  appendEntry(target, entry, events)
  appendEntryWithUsage(target, entry, record, usage, events)
}

class ExecutionTargetDTO {
  sessionId
  executionId
  rootEventId
  segmentId
}

interface RuntimeExecutionControlRepository {
  register(target, triggerEventSeq, acceptedAt)
  requestInterrupt(sessionId, targetEventId, eventId, acceptedAt)
  markConfirming(target, toolCallId, appender, terminalAt)
  acceptConfirmation(sessionId, toolCallId, eventId, segmentId, result, appender, acceptedAt)
  claimConfirmation(confirmingTarget, toolCallId, claimedAt)
  acknowledgeConfirmation(decision, completedAt)
  markTerminal(target, eventId, appender, reason, terminalAt)
  appendToSegment(target, appender)
  findCommittedTerminal(target, eventId, reason)
}

interface RuntimeSessionRepository {
  acceptUserEvent(sessionId, entry, event, acceptedAt)
  appendEntry(entry, events)
  finishExecution(sessionId, terminalAt)
}

class MyBatisRuntimeExecutionControlRepository {
  markTerminal(...)
  - cancelPendingDecisions(target, terminalAt)
}
class RuntimeExecutionControlMapper {
  markTerminal(...)
  cancelPendingConfirmations(sessionId, executionId, terminalAt)
  cancelPendingPlanConfirmations(sessionId, executionId, terminalAt)
  cancelPendingQuestionAnswers(sessionId, executionId, terminalAt)
}

entity "t_session_executions" as t_session_executions {
  session_id
  execution_id
  root_event_id
  state
  current_segment_id
}

entity "t_session_execution_segments" as t_session_execution_segments {
  segment_id
  segment_ordinal
  trigger_event_id
  state
  terminal_event_id
}

entity "t_session_execution_segment_events" as t_session_execution_segment_events {
  segment_id
  event_id
  event_seq
}

entity "t_session_tool_confirmations" as t_session_tool_confirmations {
  confirmation_event_id
  previous_segment_id
  segment_id
  tool_call_id
  result
  state
  claimed_at
  completed_at
}

entity "t_session_plan_confirmations" as t_session_plan_confirmations {
  confirmation_event_id
  target_event_id
  state
  claimed_at
  completed_at
}

entity "t_session_question_answers" as t_session_question_answers {
  answer_event_id
  target_event_id
  state
  claimed_at
  completed_at
}

entity "t_sessions" as t_sessions
entity "t_session_entries" as t_session_entries
entity "t_session_events" as t_session_events
entity "t_session_event_projection" as t_session_event_projection

RuntimeExecutionPersistenceService --> ExecutionTargetDTO
RuntimeExecutionPersistenceService --> RuntimeExecutionControlRepository
RuntimeExecutionPersistenceService --> RuntimeSessionRepository
RuntimeExecutionControlRepository <|.. MyBatisRuntimeExecutionControlRepository
MyBatisRuntimeExecutionControlRepository --> RuntimeExecutionControlMapper
RuntimeExecutionControlMapper --> t_session_executions
RuntimeExecutionControlMapper --> t_session_execution_segments
RuntimeExecutionControlMapper --> t_session_execution_segment_events
RuntimeExecutionControlMapper --> t_session_tool_confirmations
RuntimeExecutionControlMapper --> t_session_plan_confirmations
RuntimeExecutionControlMapper --> t_session_question_answers
RuntimeSessionRepository --> t_sessions
RuntimeSessionRepository --> t_session_entries
RuntimeSessionRepository --> t_session_events
RuntimeSessionRepository --> t_session_event_projection
t_session_executions ||--|{ t_session_execution_segments
t_session_execution_segments ||--o{ t_session_execution_segment_events
t_session_execution_segments ||--o| t_session_tool_confirmations
t_session_execution_segments ||--o| t_session_plan_confirmations
t_session_execution_segments ||--o| t_session_question_answers
t_session_events ||--o| t_session_execution_segment_events

note bottom of RuntimeExecutionPersistenceService
  One outer Spring transaction
  locks Session and exact execution before terminal append.
  Interrupt receipts are not linked to the message segment.
  A committed stop prevents confirmation accept or claim.
  Segment append requires same Session and current OPEN segment.
  Exact terminal retries restore original data without new writes.
  Terminal commit cancels PENDING decisions in all three tables.
  The session and execution IDs bound the update across all segments.
  CLAIMED and COMPLETED records keep their original state.
end note
@enduml

@startuml runtime_decision_consumption_state
title Durable Decision Consumption State
' Java baseline: pi-mono-java 74f1b8314c9a5eb3d1659dfed2ab90b787dd647f plus companion change
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/session/ToolConfirmationState.java
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/MyBatisRuntimeExecutionControlRepository.java#markTerminal/cancelPendingDecisions
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/resources/mapper/session/RuntimeExecutionControlMapper.xml#cancelPendingConfirmations/cancelPendingPlanConfirmations/cancelPendingQuestionAnswers
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/resources/db/gaussdb/install/session_schema.sql
' Observed behavior: claims require RUNNING and no committed stop request.
' Design reason: terminal execution and unclaimed-decision cancellation share one transaction.
' Java divergence: CANCELED ends consumption; it does not retract accepted user decisions.
hide empty description
[*] --> PENDING : accept and persist user decision
PENDING --> CLAIMED : claim once while execution can run
CLAIMED --> COMPLETED : acknowledge handling
PENDING --> CANCELED : execution commits TERMINAL\n(done, failed, terminated)
COMPLETED --> [*]
CANCELED --> [*]
note right of PENDING
  STOPPING blocks claims but keeps PENDING.
  CONFIRMING closes a segment, not the execution.
end note
note right of CANCELED
  claimed_at stays NULL.
  completed_at equals execution.terminal_at.
  Accepted input and public receipt remain stored.
  Terminal retries retain the original timestamp.
end note
note bottom of CLAIMED
  Terminal commit does not cancel claimed decisions.
  Their existing acknowledgement may still complete.
end note
@enduml
